{"title":"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Quick_Summary)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Quick Summary)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two distinct lines pass through the center of three concentric circles of radii 3, 2, and 1. The area of the shaded region in the diagram is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbdd6533c2882af567cedd2174829ff136094530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the area of the unshaded region. What is the radian measure of the acute angle formed by the two lines? (Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> radian is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/b/5cb1b41850ab676e4d1cf15c69b1609af4befbc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> degree.)\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/9/fe9afaa1f9ed8ef23f107f3e17a274aa0a17aeb3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(85); fill((-30,0)..(-24,18)--(0,0)--(-24,-18)..cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((30,0)..(24,18)--(0,0)--(24,-18)..cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((-20,0)..(0,20)--(0,-20)..cycle,white); fill((20,0)..(0,20)--(0,-20)..cycle,white); fill((0,20)..(-16,12)--(0,0)--(16,12)..cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((0,-20)..(-16,-12)--(0,0)--(16,-12)..cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((0,10)..(-10,0)--(10,0)..cycle,white); fill((0,-10)..(-10,0)--(10,0)..cycle,white); fill((-10,0)..(-8,6)--(0,0)--(-8,-6)..cycle,gray(0.7)); fill((10,0)..(8,6)--(0,0)--(8,-6)..cycle,gray(0.7)); draw(Circle((0,0),10),linewidth(0.7)); draw(Circle((0,0),20),linewidth(0.7)); draw(Circle((0,0),30),linewidth(0.7)); draw((-28,-21)--(28,21),linewidth(0.7)); draw((-28,21)--(28,-21),linewidth(0.7));[/asy]\" width=\"142\" height=\"142\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/f/1df956a70f1ecade85c32aa0066c86f1e185beea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{7} \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{5} \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"370\" height=\"33\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the area of the shaded region be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, the area of the unshaded region be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, and the acute angle that is formed by the two lines be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. We can set up two equations between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbebb3bd73f1ae5c64098ab0244f739abf7ca4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/4/3e44785cc8aae3adf6be4ee99857eeb3435e11b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S+U=9\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/113c122232a1da59c862a1efd02a5cb552f70066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\dfrac{8}{13}U$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"72\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/4/fc4d137c4d99eaa5b2d67fbc6cd754b0f51ab1a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{21}{13}U=9\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/f/96f54ecb8d87e257c9ac556391f08baea6a2c9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U=\\dfrac{39\\pi}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206d36902ac866bf1dbfbfb89918322b71d39b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=\\dfrac{8}{13}\\cdot \\dfrac{39\\pi}{7}=\\dfrac{24\\pi}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Now we can make a formula for the area of the shaded region in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece80f6b5630e09d3829014f41c5b7948f866379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{2\\theta}{2\\pi} \\cdot \\pi +\\dfrac{2(\\pi-\\theta)}{2\\pi} \\cdot (4\\pi-\\pi)+\\dfrac{2\\theta}{2\\pi}(9\\pi-4\\pi)=\\theta +3\\pi-3\\theta+5\\theta=3\\theta+3\\pi=\\dfrac{24\\pi}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"640\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/171167538f988273e44a2178d63880d4416f47f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{7}\\Rightarrow \\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{7}\\Rightarrow\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\pi}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"230\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As mentioned in Solution #1, we can make an equation for the area of the shaded region in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659ee0f6d4069d2d3f020c986608fb94a85784f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies\\dfrac{2\\theta}{2\\pi} \\cdot \\pi +\\dfrac{2(\\pi-\\theta)}{2\\pi} \\cdot (4\\pi-\\pi)+\\dfrac{2\\theta}{2\\pi}(9\\pi-4\\pi)=\\theta +3\\pi-3\\theta+5\\theta=3\\theta+3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"628\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>So, the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a19d5d9c7796bfa25b566b6d79e3cc62ea99a923.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta+3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />. This means that the unshaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/0/080ddb0a93c63663aebe4f1d636defbe6f397f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\pi-(3\\theta+3\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Also, the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbdd6533c2882af567cedd2174829ff136094530.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8}{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> of the unshaded region. Hence, we can now make an equation and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0dc82c5491d83fba64e802b51ae8bbf919658e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\theta+3\\pi=\\frac{8}{13}(9\\pi-(3\\theta+3\\pi)\\implies 39\\theta+39\\pi=8(6\\pi-3\\theta)\\implies 39\\theta+39\\pi=48\\pi-24\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"697\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c84bec6f976f4fe77fa07081417cb6fabe0a249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$63\\theta=9\\pi\\implies \\theta=\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{\\pi}{7}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"213\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Quick_Summary.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Quick_Summary)\">Solution 3 (Quick Summary)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Quick Summary)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can find the area of the shaded region, which turns out to be 24π/7. Then, we can set θ to be the acute angle. We get  6(θ)+3(180-θ)=(Area of shaded region). After we simplify, we get  θ=π/7. Simplifying, we get (B)==&gt;π/7. (If you have limited time and you find the area of the shaded region, you could make an educated guess and go for π/7 since the denominator is 7).\n</p><p>~Unknown Editor (stupid)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/t3EWtMnJu2Y?t=49\">https://youtu.be/t3EWtMnJu2Y?t=49</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A\">2004 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 234/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6072/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.820      1 -total\n 58.79%    8.125      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 40.17%    5.551      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5561:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 2